      "side": 1,
      "message": "is \u0027+\u0027 a good deliminator after a hostname? What about putting the fixed part first (i.e. \"token/example.com\") so that any odd characters in the hostname don\u0027t get confused? Also if you always include a prefix, there\u0027s no possibility of confusion with ECDSA (i.e. untagged) hostnames, although that will invalidate existing caches.",
