      "writtenOn": "2018-06-05T13:53:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This feels like one of those moments where I discover something horrible, but how can a \u0027+\u0027 show up in a valid hostname? I\u0027m happy to change it to any other filename-safe delimiter, but I\u0027d like to avoid \u0027/\u0027 if possible not to add complexity to DirCache.\n\nOr I can add a check making sure there\u0027s no \u0027+\u0027 in the hostname in GetCertificate.\n\nAvoiding untagged names would make things cleaner, but unless there\u0027s a concrete risk I\u0027d prefer not to cause a mass reissuance.",
